---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import DeskBootPreview from '../components/DeskBootPreview.astro'
import DeskMedia from '../components/DeskMedia.astro'
import { ogPathFor } from '../data/og'
import { deskHosts, labelFor, allowedLabels } from '../data/readiness.mjs'
import { deskSetupUrl, factoryUrl, rfcUrl } from '../data/principles.mjs'

const title = 'Desk: where my agents keep their work | Ouro'
const description = 'Desk keeps the principles in the setup: your agent’s work lives in a Git repository you own, every job starts with one alignment conversation, and a job is done when you’ve seen it work. For Claude Code and GitHub Copilot CLI, with Crew for teams.'
const status = labelFor('desk-claude-code-macos')
const hosted = labelFor('desk-hosted')
// The three Claude Code hosts share the page's label, so they collapse into one row.
const otherHosts = deskHosts.filter((host) => !host.id.startsWith('desk-claude-code-'))
const supportPrompt = 'Something went wrong with Desk. Look at what happened in this session, then file a GitHub issue on ourostack/desk with the steps to reproduce it and the exact error. Show me the issue before you submit it.'
const link = 'text-scale underline underline-offset-4 decoration-scale/40 hover:text-glow hover:decoration-current hover:decoration-2 transition-colors'
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} ogImage={ogPathFor('/desk')} canonical="https://ouroboros.bot/desk/">
  <section class="px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-16 pt-32 pb-10 md:pt-44">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto grid gap-10 xl:grid-cols-[1.2fr_1fr]">
      <div class="grid gap-5 content-start min-w-0">
        <span class={`tag ${status.tone} justify-self-start`}>{status.label}</span>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
          <img src="/brand/desk-render.webp" srcset="/brand/desk-render-128.webp 128w, /brand/desk-render-256.webp 256w, /brand/desk-render.webp 1024w" sizes="(min-width: 768px) 64px, 56px" width="64" height="64" alt="" class="mark-render w-14 h-14 md:w-16 md:h-16" />
          <h1 class="heading-lead">Desk</h1>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xl md:text-2xl text-bone font-display leading-snug">Desk keeps my agents' work in a Git repository: every track, task, decision, and lesson. I can open any harness on any of my machines, ask "where were we?", and the agent knows.</p>
        <p class="text-lg text-mist leading-relaxed">Every job starts with one conversation and a go, and ends with evidence you accept or send back, the way <a href="/approach/" class={link}>How I work</a> lays it out. The full design is in <a href={rfcUrl} class={link}>Desk's design doc</a>.</p>

        <div class="grid gap-2">
          <span class="caption-mono">Give your agent</span>
          <pre id="desk-setup" class="agent-text">{`${deskSetupUrl}\nset this up`}</pre>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
            <button type="button" data-copy-target="desk-setup" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-xl bg-bone text-void px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-scale transition-colors"><span data-copy-label>Copy</span></button>
            <span class="sr-only">In words: give your agent {deskSetupUrl} and say "set this up".</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-mist">Setup also installs <a href="https://github.com/obra/superpowers" class={link}>Superpowers</a>, Jesse Vincent's skill set for coding agents. Desk asks once whether you'd like to send your sessions' timings to the public <a href={factoryUrl} class={link}>factory</a>. It sends timings and sizes, and never transcript text, prompts, file contents, or names.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="min-w-0">
        <DeskMedia />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-16 py-12 border-t border-canopy/15">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto grid gap-5">
      <h2 class="heading-sub">Where it runs</h2>
      <ul class="grid gap-4">
        <li>
          <span class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3"><span class="text-lg text-bone">Claude Code</span><span class={`tag ${status.tone}`}>{status.label}</span></span>
          <span class="block text-mist">macOS: tested daily. Linux and Windows: the full test suite runs on both in CI.</span>
        </li>
        {otherHosts.map((host) => (
          <li>
            <span class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3"><span class="text-lg text-bone">{host.name}</span><span class={`tag ${allowedLabels[host.label]}`}>{host.label}</span></span>
            <span class="block text-mist">{host.detail}{/[.!?]$/.test(host.detail) ? '' : '.'}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <h2 class="heading-sub mt-8">Known limits today</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 grid gap-2 text-lg text-mist">
        <li>Desk's own browser starts signed out, and on macOS it can steal focus.</li>
        <li>We haven't yet tested a first install on a brand-new Mac account.</li>
        <li>Turning reported problems into fixes is built, and it hasn't been proven on real work yet.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-16 py-12 border-t border-canopy/15">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto grid gap-6">
      <h2 class="heading-sub">What a new session looks like</h2>
      <figure class="grid gap-3 min-w-0">
        <DeskBootPreview />
        <figcaption class="text-sm text-mist">A new session picks up where the last one left off. This is real output from Desk's session start, run on a sample desk: every task, its state, and its next step or blocker, before anyone asks.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <h2 class="heading-sub mt-8">Support goes through your agent</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-mist">Give your agent this:</p>
      <pre id="desk-support" class="agent-text">{supportPrompt}</pre>
      <button type="button" data-copy-target="desk-support" class="justify-self-start inline-flex items-center rounded-xl border border-canopy text-bone px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:border-scale hover:text-scale transition-colors"><span data-copy-label>Copy</span></button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="crew" class="px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-16 py-12 border-t border-canopy/15 scroll-mt-16">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto grid gap-5">
      <h2 class="heading-sub">Crew: one repository for a whole team</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-mist leading-relaxed">Desk is one person's workspace. Crew turns one repository into a shared workspace for several people and their agents. Everyone reads all of it, and each person's agents write only in that person's own desk, so work from many hands merges cleanly.</p>
      <p class="text-lg text-mist leading-relaxed">Facts, one person's view, and what the team actually decided each have their own place. Ask an agent what a teammate thinks, or what was agreed, and it answers from the right place and says whose view it is.</p>
      <p class="text-mist">Crew is a separate plugin, <code class="model-code">crew@ourostack</code>, from the same marketplace as Desk. See the <a href="https://github.com/ourostack/desk/blob/main/plugins/crew/README.md" class={link}>Crew guide</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="hosted" class="px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-16 py-12 border-t border-canopy/15 scroll-mt-16">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto grid gap-5">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <h2 class="heading-sub">Hosted Desk on claude.ai</h2>
        <span class={`tag ${hosted.tone}`}>{hosted.label}</span>
      </div>
      <p class="text-lg text-mist leading-relaxed">Hosted Desk lets claude.ai use Desk as a remote connector, so a chat in the browser can pick up the same work. Sign-in is by invitation for now. Tools that need a shell or a coding harness stay with your local agent.</p>
      <figure class="grid gap-2">
        <img src="/images/workshop/hosted-desk-connected.webp" width="1200" height="804" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="claude.ai connector settings showing Desk connected at desk.ouro.bot/mcp, with its read-only tools listed and each set to need approval." class="w-full h-auto rounded-xl border border-canopy/40" />
        <figcaption class="text-sm text-mist">Desk connected in claude.ai, shown with the current Desk logo.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
